IMPORT prelude

-- Merchant Shipping Act 1995 (Singapore) -- limitation of shipowners' liability for maritime claims (Part 8, ss 135 to 138, and
-- Articles 1 to 4, 6 and 7 of the 1976 Limitation Convention in the First Schedule); four safety duties of owners and masters
-- (Part 5, ss 98, 102, 106 and 107); and the duties of a person who finds wreck and what happens to it (Part 9, ss 153, 156, 157,
-- 159).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MSA1995.txt, with amendments
-- to Act 9 of 2026 (in force 1 May 2026) shown. Section numbers follow the BODY of the deposit; the arrangement of sections at the
-- top of the deposit has its numbers shifted against the titles (e.g. "1." stands beside "Exemption of naval ships").
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 17 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the provisions with decision content
-- that a shipowner, master, insurer, claimant or member of the public actually meets. Not encoded: registration, mortgages and
-- transfers (Part 2), manning and certification (Part 3), crew matters including wages and discipline (Part 4), survey,
-- certificates, load lines and unsafe ships (rest of Part 5), inquiries (Part 6), delivery of goods and liens (Part 7), the
-- limitation fund, distribution and bar to other actions (Articles 9 to 14, ss 139, 140), salvage awards and the Salvage Convention
-- (s 145A, ss 166 onwards and Second Schedule), legal proceedings (Part 10) and everything left to regulations or orders.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Merchant Shipping Act 1995 -- liability, safety duties, wreck`

-- Helpers (the prelude has no min/max).
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- The number of tons of `tonnage` that fall in the band starting after `from` and `width` tons wide.
GIVEN `tonnage` IS A NUMBER, `from` IS A NUMBER, `width` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tons in the band` MEANS
    IF `tonnage` AT MOST `from` THEN 0
    ELSE `the lesser of` (`tonnage` MINUS `from`) `width`

§ `Part 8 -- limitation of liability for maritime claims`

§§ `Article 1 and s 136(4) -- who may limit`

-- Art 1(1): "Shipowners and salvors ... may limit their liability". (2): "shipowner" means "the owner, charterer, manager and
-- operator of a seagoing ship". (4): a person "for whose act, neglect or default the shipowner or salvor is responsible" may also
-- limit. (6): "An insurer of liability ... shall be entitled to the benefits of this Convention to the same extent as the assured".
-- s 136(4): "Despite paragraph 2 of Article 1 ... the right to limit liability ... applies in relation to any ship whether seagoing
-- or not". So whether the ship is seagoing makes no difference in Singapore.
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `the registered owner`
    `a charterer`
    `a manager`
    `an operator`
    `a salvor`
    `a liability insurer`
    `the master or a crew member`
    `the owner of the cargo`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the ship is seagoing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may invoke limitation` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `the owner of the cargo` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Articles 2, 3 and 4 and s 136(1), (2) -- which claims may be limited`

-- Art 2(1): subject to limitation "whatever the basis of liability may be": (a) loss of life, personal injury, loss of or damage to
-- property "(including damage to harbour works, basins and waterways and aids to navigation)"; (b) delay in carriage by sea; (c)
-- infringement of rights "other than contractual rights"; (d) raising or removal of a sunk, wrecked, stranded or abandoned ship;
-- (e) removal of the cargo; (f) claims of a third person for measures taken to avert or minimise loss.
-- s 136(1): the Convention has the force of law "other than paragraph 1(d) and (e) of Article 2". So wreck-raising and
-- cargo-removal claims cannot be limited in Singapore.
-- Art 2(2), read with s 136(2)(b): a 1(f) claim is not limited "to the extent that [it relates] to remuneration under a contract
-- with the person liable".
-- Art 3: the Convention does not apply to (a) salvage, special compensation or contribution in general average; (b) oil pollution
-- damage under the 1969 Civil Liability Convention; (c), (d) nuclear damage. (Art 3(e), crew claims, turns on the law of the
-- contract of service and is not encoded.)
-- Art 4: no limitation "if it is proved that the loss resulted from his personal act or omission, committed with the intent to
-- cause such loss, or recklessly and with knowledge that such loss would probably result".
DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `loss of life or personal injury`
    `damage to property`
    `damage to harbour works`
    `loss from delay in carriage by sea`
    `infringement of non-contractual rights`
    `raising or removing a sunk or wrecked ship`
    `removing the ship's cargo`
    `measures by another person to avert or minimise loss`
    `salvage`
    `contribution in general average`
    `oil pollution damage`
    `nuclear damage`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim, `the claim is remuneration under a contract with the person liable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is of a limitable kind` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `loss of life or personal injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `damage to property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `damage to harbour works` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `loss from delay in carriage by sea` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `infringement of non-contractual rights` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `measures by another person to avert or minimise loss` THEN NOT `the claim is remuneration under a contract with the person liable`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim, `the claim is remuneration under a contract with the person liable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `intentional or reckless personal conduct is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `liability for the claim may be limited` IF
        `the claim is of a limitable kind` `the claim` `the claim is remuneration under a contract with the person liable`
    AND (NOT `intentional or reckless personal conduct is proved`)

§§ `Article 6 and s 137 -- the general limits`

-- Art 6(1)(a), loss of life or personal injury: (i) "3.02 million Units of Account for a ship with a tonnage not exceeding 2,000
-- tons"; (ii) in addition, for each ton from 2,001 to 30,000, 1,208; from 30,001 to 70,000, 906; in excess of 70,000, 604.
-- Art 6(1)(b), any other claims: (i) 1.51 million; (ii) 604, 453, 302 per ton on the same bands.
-- s 137(1)(b): for a ship (other than a licensed harbour craft) "with a tonnage less than 300 tons", (a)(i) is read as 166,667 Units
-- of Account and (b)(i) as 83,333. (2): tonnage is gross tonnage.
-- Note the cliff: a 299-ton ship limits personal-injury claims at 166,667 Units; a 300-ton ship at 3.02 million.
-- Art 8: the Unit of Account is the IMF Special Drawing Right; s 142 lets the Authority certify the Singapore dollar equivalent.
-- The figures here are in Units of Account; no conversion is modelled.
GIVEN `tonnage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the personal injury limit` MEANS
    IF `tonnage` LESS THAN 300 THEN 166667
    ELSE 3020000
         PLUS `the tons in the band` `tonnage` 2000 28000 TIMES 1208
         PLUS `the tons in the band` `tonnage` 30000 40000 TIMES 906
         PLUS `the tons in the band` `tonnage` 70000 1000000000 TIMES 604

GIVEN `tonnage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the other claims limit` MEANS
    IF `tonnage` LESS THAN 300 THEN 83333
    ELSE 1510000
         PLUS `the tons in the band` `tonnage` 2000 28000 TIMES 604
         PLUS `the tons in the band` `tonnage` 30000 40000 TIMES 453
         PLUS `the tons in the band` `tonnage` 70000 1000000000 TIMES 302

-- s 137(1)(a): for a ship licensed as a harbour craft, Article 6 has effect "as if the aggregate of the amounts in paragraph
-- 1(a)(i) and (b)(i) referred to the sum insured under the policy of insurance ... required by the Port Master ... in respect of
-- third party risks". Only the (i) amounts are replaced; the per-ton additions above 2,000 tons are kept (a reading of the text;
-- how the sum insured is split between (a) and (b) is not said).
GIVEN `tonnage` IS A NUMBER, `licensed harbour craft` IS A BOOLEAN, `the third-party sum insured` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the aggregate general limit` MEANS
    IF `licensed harbour craft`
    THEN `the third-party sum insured`
         PLUS (`the personal injury limit` (`the greater of` `tonnage` 2000) MINUS 3020000)
         PLUS (`the other claims limit` (`the greater of` `tonnage` 2000) MINUS 1510000)
    ELSE `the personal injury limit` `tonnage` PLUS `the other claims limit` `tonnage`

-- Art 6(4): the limits for "any salvor not operating from any ship or for any salvor operating solely on the ship to ... which he
-- is rendering salvage services, shall be calculated according to a tonnage of 1,500 tons".
GIVEN `the salvor's own tonnage` IS A NUMBER, `operating from a ship of its own` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the salvor's limitation tonnage` MEANS
    IF `operating from a ship of its own` THEN `the salvor's own tonnage` ELSE 1500

-- Art 6(2): where the 1(a) amount "is insufficient to pay the claims mentioned therein in full, the amount calculated in accordance
-- with paragraph 1(b) shall be available for payment of the unpaid balance of claims under paragraph 1(a) and such unpaid balance
-- shall rank rateably with claims mentioned under paragraph 1(b)".
-- (s 136(3) gives harbour-works claims priority over other 1(b) claims; that priority is not modelled here.)
GIVEN `tonnage` IS A NUMBER, `personal injury claims` IS A NUMBER, `other claims` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the unpaid personal injury balance` MEANS
    `the greater of` 0 (`personal injury claims` MINUS `the personal injury limit` `tonnage`)

GIVEN `tonnage` IS A NUMBER, `personal injury claims` IS A NUMBER, `other claims` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the recovery of personal injury claimants` MEANS
    IF `the unpaid personal injury balance` `tonnage` `personal injury claims` `other claims` PLUS `other claims`
         AT MOST `the other claims limit` `tonnage`
    THEN `personal injury claims`
    ELSE `the lesser of` `personal injury claims` (`the personal injury limit` `tonnage`)
         PLUS (`the other claims limit` `tonnage`
               TIMES `the unpaid personal injury balance` `tonnage` `personal injury claims` `other claims`
               DIVIDED BY (`the unpaid personal injury balance` `tonnage` `personal injury claims` `other claims` PLUS `other claims`))

GIVEN `tonnage` IS A NUMBER, `personal injury claims` IS A NUMBER, `other claims` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the recovery of other claimants` MEANS
    IF `the unpaid personal injury balance` `tonnage` `personal injury claims` `other claims` PLUS `other claims`
         AT MOST `the other claims limit` `tonnage`
    THEN `other claims`
    ELSE `the other claims limit` `tonnage` TIMES `other claims`
         DIVIDED BY (`the unpaid personal injury balance` `tonnage` `personal injury claims` `other claims` PLUS `other claims`)

§§ `Article 7 and s 138 -- passenger claims`

-- Art 7(1): for loss of life or personal injury to passengers, the limit is "175,000 Units of Account multiplied by the number of
-- passengers that the ship is authorised to carry according to the ship's certificate". s 138: for a passenger ship that
-- certificate is "the passenger ship's certificate issued under or recognised by regulations made under section 100".
-- The limit turns on the number AUTHORISED, not the number actually on board.
GIVEN `passengers authorised by the certificate` IS A NUMBER, `passengers actually carried` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the passenger claims limit` MEANS
    175000 TIMES `passengers authorised by the certificate`

§§ `135 -- exclusion of liability for fire and undeclared valuables`

-- s 135(1): the owner of a Singapore ship "is not liable for any loss or damage" (a) "where any property on board the ship is lost
-- or damaged by reason of fire on board the ship"; or (b) where "gold, silver, watches, jewels or precious stones" are lost or
-- damaged by theft, robbery or other dishonest conduct "and their nature and value were not at the time of shipment declared ... in
-- the bill of lading or otherwise in writing". (3): this does not exclude liability for a personal act or omission of the kind in
-- Article 4. (4): "owner" includes any part owner, charterer, manager or operator.
-- This is a complete exclusion, not a limit -- and it applies only to Singapore ships.
DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
    `fire on board`
    `theft or other dishonesty`
    `some other cause`

GIVEN `a Singapore ship` IS A BOOLEAN, `the cause` IS A Cause, `the goods are gold, silver, watches, jewels or precious stones` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `nature and value declared in writing at shipment` IS A BOOLEAN, `intentional or reckless personal conduct is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner's liability is excluded` IF
        `a Singapore ship`
    AND (NOT `intentional or reckless personal conduct is proved`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the cause`
         WHEN `fire on board` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `theft or other dishonesty` THEN `the goods are gold, silver, watches, jewels or precious stones` AND (NOT `nature and value declared in writing at shipment`)
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

§ `Part 5 -- survey and safety`

§§ `98 -- ships to which Part 5 applies`

-- s 98: "This Part, unless otherwise provided, applies to all Singapore ships wherever they may be and to all ships in Singapore
-- except harbour craft." Read here with the harbour-craft exception attaching to ships in Singapore that are not Singapore ships;
-- the sentence could also be read as excepting every harbour craft (see NOTES).
GIVEN `a Singapore ship` IS A BOOLEAN, `in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `a harbour craft` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 5 applies to the ship` IF
        `a Singapore ship`
    OR  (`in Singapore` AND (NOT `a harbour craft`))

§§ `102 -- carrying passengers in excess`

-- s 2: "passenger ship" means "a ship which carries more than 12 passengers".
-- s 102(1): the owner or master of a passenger ship "must not carry or receive on board ... any number of passengers which ... is
-- greater than the number allowed by the passenger ship's safety certificate": fine up to $10,000 or imprisonment up to 2 years or
-- both. (2): the Director or Port Master may detain the ship until it complies.
GIVEN `passengers carried` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ship is a passenger ship` IF
    `passengers carried` GREATER THAN 12

GIVEN `passengers carried` IS A NUMBER, `passengers allowed by the safety certificate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carrying excess passengers is an offence` IF
        `the ship is a passenger ship` `passengers carried`
    AND `passengers carried` GREATER THAN `passengers allowed by the safety certificate`

§§ `106 -- duty to assist after a collision`

-- s 106(1): "In every case of collision between 2 ships", the master (or person in charge) of EACH ship must, "if and so far as he or
-- she can do so without danger to his or her own ship, crew and passengers", (a) render practicable assistance and stand by, and
-- (b) give the other ship his or her ship's name, port of registry, and ports of origin and destination.
-- (2): a master who "without reasonable cause" fails to comply: fine up to $10,000, and a certificated officer may face an inquiry
-- and lose the certificate.
GIVEN `a collision between 2 ships` IS A BOOLEAN, `can assist without danger to own ship, crew and passengers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the master must assist and stand by` IF
    `a collision between 2 ships` AND `can assist without danger to own ship, crew and passengers`

GIVEN `a collision between 2 ships` IS A BOOLEAN, `can assist without danger to own ship, crew and passengers` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `assisted and gave particulars` IS A BOOLEAN, `had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the master commits the collision offence` IF
        `the master must assist and stand by` `a collision between 2 ships` `can assist without danger to own ship, crew and passengers`
    AND (NOT `assisted and gave particulars`)
    AND (NOT `had reasonable cause`)

§§ `107 -- reporting accidents to the Director within 24 hours`

-- s 107(1): where a ship (a) "has sustained or caused an accident occasioning loss of life or serious injury"; (b) has sustained
-- an accident, damage, defect or deficiency that "has affected, or is likely to affect the seaworthiness of the ship, or the
-- efficiency or completeness of the lifesaving appliances or other safety equipment"; (c) "has been in a position of great peril";
-- or (d) "has been stranded or wrecked", the owner or master "must, within 24 hours of the happening, report the happening to the
-- Director". (2): not a matter required to be reported under s 4 of the Merchant Shipping (Wreck Removal) Act 2017. (3): failure
-- "without reasonable cause": fine up to $10,000.
DECLARE Happening IS ONE OF
    `an accident causing death or serious injury`
    `damage affecting seaworthiness or safety equipment`
    `damage not affecting seaworthiness or safety equipment`
    `a position of great peril`
    `stranding or wreck`

GIVEN `the happening` IS A Happening, `reportable under the Wreck Removal Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the happening must be reported to the Director` IF
        (NOT `reportable under the Wreck Removal Act`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the happening`
         WHEN `damage not affecting seaworthiness or safety equipment` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

GIVEN `the happening` IS A Happening, `reportable under the Wreck Removal Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `hours until reported` IS A NUMBER,
      `had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to report the happening is an offence` IF
        `the happening must be reported to the Director` `the happening` `reportable under the Wreck Removal Act`
    AND `hours until reported` GREATER THAN 24
    AND (NOT `had reasonable cause`)

§ `Part 9 -- wreck`

§§ `153 -- duties of a person who finds wreck`

-- s 145: "wreck" includes "jetsam, flotsam, lagan and derelict found in or on the shores of the sea or any tidal water".
-- s 153(1): a person who finds or takes possession of wreck within Singapore (or brings it in) must (a) "if the person is the owner
-- thereof, give notice to the receiver ... describing the marks by which the wreck may be recognised"; or (b) "if the person is not
-- the owner thereof, as soon as possible deliver the wreck to the receiver".
-- (2): failure "without reasonable cause": fine up to $2,000 and, "if the person is not the owner", the person ALSO forfeits any
-- claim to salvage and must pay "double the value" of the wreck to its owner (or, if unclaimed, to the person entitled to it).
DECLARE FinderDuty IS ONE OF
    `give notice to the receiver`
    `deliver the wreck to the receiver`

GIVEN `the finder owns the wreck` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A FinderDuty
`the finder's duty` MEANS
    IF `the finder owns the wreck` THEN `give notice to the receiver` ELSE `deliver the wreck to the receiver`

GIVEN `the finder owns the wreck` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied` IS A BOOLEAN, `had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the finder commits an offence` IF
    (NOT `complied`) AND (NOT `had reasonable cause`)

GIVEN `the finder owns the wreck` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied` IS A BOOLEAN, `had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the finder forfeits any claim to salvage` IF
        `the finder commits an offence` `the finder owns the wreck` `complied` `had reasonable cause`
    AND (NOT `the finder owns the wreck`)

GIVEN `the finder owns the wreck` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied` IS A BOOLEAN, `had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN, `value of the wreck` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the double value the finder must pay` MEANS
    IF `the finder forfeits any claim to salvage` `the finder owns the wreck` `complied` `had reasonable cause`
    THEN 2 TIMES `value of the wreck`
    ELSE 0

§§ `156, 157 and 159 -- what happens to wreck held by the receiver`

-- s 157(1): the receiver "may at any time sell any wreck in his or her custody" if in his or her opinion (a) "it is under the value
-- of $1,000"; (b) it is so damaged or perishable that it cannot with advantage be kept; or (c) it is not of sufficient value to pay
-- for warehousing. (2): the proceeds stand in place of the wreck.
GIVEN `value of the wreck` IS A NUMBER, `damaged or perishable` IS A BOOLEAN, `not worth warehousing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the receiver may sell at once` IF
    `value of the wreck` LESS THAN 1000 OR `damaged or perishable` OR `not worth warehousing`

-- s 156(1): the owner, "upon establishing the owner's claim to the wreck to the satisfaction of the receiver within one month from
-- the time at which the wreck came into the possession of the receiver, is entitled, upon paying the salvage fees and expenses
-- due, to have the wreck or the proceeds thereof delivered up". s 159(1): where no owner establishes a claim within one month,
-- "the receiver must sell the wreck" and pay the proceeds (less expenses, fees and salvage) "into the Consolidated Fund". s 158:
-- the Government is entitled to all unclaimed wreck, except where it has granted the right to another.
-- Time is counted here in whole days, taking one month as 30 days (an assumption: the Act does not define the month).
DECLARE WreckOutcome IS ONE OF
    `delivered to the owner on paying salvage fees and expenses`
    `sold, proceeds to the Consolidated Fund`

GIVEN `an owner established a claim` IS A BOOLEAN, `days after the receiver took possession` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A WreckOutcome
`what becomes of the wreck` MEANS
    IF `an owner established a claim` AND `days after the receiver took possession` AT MOST 30
    THEN `delivered to the owner on paying salvage fees and expenses`
    ELSE `sold, proceeds to the Consolidated Fund`

§ `Maximum penalties`

-- ss 102(1), 106(2), 107(3), 153(2) as quoted above.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `carrying excess passengers`
    `failing to assist after a collision`
    `failing to report an accident`
    `failing to notify or deliver wreck`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `carrying excess passengers` THEN 10000
    WHEN `failing to assist after a collision` THEN 10000
    WHEN `failing to report an accident` THEN 10000
    OTHERWISE 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `carrying excess passengers` THEN 24
    OTHERWISE 0
